     DETAILED DESCRIPTION 
     The object of this invention was to discover a selective cPLA 2  inhibitor which is active, both topically and orally, in treating inflammary disease of the skin and other tissues as well as other chronic and acute conditions which have been linked to inappropriate activation of the cPLA 2  enzymes. Preferably such compound would also be devoid of undesirable lipid-perturbing activities associated with skin irritation. 
     The above-mentioned objectives have been met by the compounds of formula I described above. 
